id: pmc-ny9i
title: Add opt-in Dependabot dependency sections so item-less release windows still get notes
description: "Dependency-only releases get empty changelog. Add opt-in --dependency-updates flag. Companion: pm-cli-website-tbni."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[2]: "area:release",release-notes
created_at: "2026-09-25T07:57:27.797Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-25T10:35:23.470Z"
deadline: "2026-09-27T00:00:00.000Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-25T09:36:50.890Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-25T09:36:50.890Z"
author: pi-agent
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: opt-in flag in cli.ts and extension.ts; Dependabot subjects in Dependencies section; Item-less windows with deps still produce sections; Without flag byte-identical; 100/100/100 coverage
resolution: Added the opt-in --dependency-updates flag to the CLI and the host extension
expected_result: "A dependency-only release gets a non-empty section listing its Dependabot bumps, and output without the flag is unchanged"
actual_result: "pm-csv v2026.09.23 renders its four bumps with PR links; coverage 100/100/100; release:check exits 0"
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pmc-an10,related,"2026-09-25T07:57:27.797Z",pi-agent,"cli:create:dep",asserted
comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-25T07:57:27.797Z",pi-agent,Starting implementation
  "2026-09-25T09:36:50.370Z",claude-hub,"Finished by the orchestrator after the pi agent hit its run time limit with 505/505 tests passing and generator.ts at 99.88% branches. The one uncovered branch was an early return for empty sections that callers never reach and that mapping an empty list already covers, so it was removed; gitCwd is now passed explicitly instead of two non-null assertions. README and docs/usage.md document the flag. Real-data acceptance: on pm-csv at tag v2026.09.23 the flag produces exactly the four Dependabot bullets hand-written for that release, in both the single-window and all-release-tags modes."
  "2026-09-25T10:22:11.755Z",claude-hub,"Review round 1 (Greptile, 8 findings, all fixed): exact tag ranges for a single release (previous..current tag from the release context, not commit dates); a pending release whose tag does not exist yet reads to HEAD; an orphaned previous tag falls back to the window's time bounds inside the newer tag's history, and to nothing without them; only 'bump' subjects count; descriptions are escaped like item titles; release and milestone grouping are refused by both CLI surfaces and left untouched by the library; --changelog-json and --summary list the bumps; pm changelog export accepts the flag. 514/514 tests, 100/100/100; release:check exits 0."
  "2026-09-25T10:35:23.470Z",claude-hub,"Review round 2 (Greptile): an explicit --until now also bounds a single release's exact tag range (tagged or pending), matching how it cuts off pm items; release-tag windows keep exact tag ranges. The new test fails without the cutoff. 515/515, 100/100/100, release:check exits 0."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-25T07:57:27.797Z",pi-agent,Opt-in to avoid stale CHANGELOG fleet-wide
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-25T07:57:27.797Z",pi-agent,Dependabot subjects follow build or chore with deps scope
